    spec:
  grid: 18-28 rows x 18-28 cols, uniform bg color
  prototypes:
    count: exactly 2 distinct small sprite patterns (proto_A, proto_B)
    shape: 3x3 to 5x5 bounding box, same shape for both
    structure: |
      Each proto is a polychrome pattern with bg holes, color-1 "anchor" cells, and 2 variable-color regions.
      Color 1 always present in both protos. Each proto has exactly 2 non-bg non-1 colors.
      Non-bg region is 8-connected. Both protos are LR-symmetric [observed].
    anchor: color-1 cells span a sub-bbox used for alignment; anchor bbox same size in both protos
    relationship: proto_B is flipUD of proto_A structurally (bg/1/other positions) [observed in 2/3, identical in 1/3]
